title: "认知语义基元三论（CSMT / CCT / CART）：同一理论 T 的三种等价公理化"
title-en: "Cognitive Semantic Primitive Trilogy (CSMT/CCT/CART): Three Equivalent Axiomatizations of One Theory T"
version: 1.0
date-released: "2026-09-16"
url: "https://gitee.com/mofahuizhang/semantic-primitive-trilogy"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21831385"
license:
  - "MulanPSL-2.0"
  - "CC-BY-NC-4.0"
abstract: >-
  A trilogy of three equivalent axiomatizations of a single theory T on cognitive semantics:
  CSMT (semantic primitive matrix, static structure), CCT (cognitive encoding, dynamic coding),
  and CART (cognitive attention resources, resource generation). CSMT and CCT start from
  axiom A0 plus postulates P1-P3; CART gives a deeper reduction from hard constraints B1
  (attention budget) and B2 (carrier separation) to A0/P1-P3. All three share one proposition
  registry (SSOT) and 19 volumes in six-volume sets per framework.
keywords:
  - "cognitive semantics"
  - "semantic primitive"
  - "attention budget"
  - "axiomatization"
  - "semantic encoding"
  - "large language models"